      "content": "#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <algorithm>\n\nstatic inline int read_int() {\n    int x = 0;\n    char c = getchar_unlocked();\n    while (c <= ' ') c = getchar_unlocked();\n    bool neg = false;\n    if (c == '-') { neg = true; c = getchar_unlocked(); }\n    while (c >= '0' && c <= '9') {\n        x = x * 10 + (c - '0');\n        c = getchar_unlocked();\n    }\n    return neg ? -x : x;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    int n = read_int();\n    int s = read_int();\n\n    const int np1 = n + 1;\n    std::vector<int> mat(n * n);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        int base = i * n;\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n            mat[base + j] = read_int();\n        }\n    }\n\n    std::vector<long long> pref(np1 * np1, 0LL);\n\n    // Horizontal pass: cumulative sums per row\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        long long row_sum = 0;\n        int base_i = (i + 1) * np1;\n        int mat_base = i * n;\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n            row_sum += mat[mat_base + j];\n            pref[base_i + (j + 1)] = row_sum;\n        }\n    }\n\n    // Vertical pass: accumulate columns to complete integral image\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        const long long *prev_row = &pref[i * np1];\n        long long *cur_row = &pref[(i + 1) * np1];\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n            cur_row[j + 1] += prev_row[j + 1];\n        }\n    }\n\n    // Search for maximum SxS submatrix sum using blocking\n    const int B = 256;\n    long long mxSum = -9223372036854775807LL - 1; // LLONG_MIN\n\n    for (int ii = 0; ii < n - s + 1; ii += B) {\n        int i_end = std::min(ii + B, n - s + 1);\n        for (int jj = 0; jj < n - s + 1; jj += B) {\n            int j_end_block = std::min(jj + B, n - s + 1);\n            for (int i = ii; i < i_end; ++i) {\n                const long long *row_i_s = &pref[(i + s) * np1];\n                const long long *row_i   = &pref[i * np1];\n                for (int j = jj; j < j_end_block; ++j) {\n                    long long sum = row_i_s[j + s] - row_i[j + s]\n                                   - row_i_s[j] + row_i[j];\n                    if (sum > mxSum) mxSum = sum;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    printf(\"%d\\n\", static_cast<int>(mxSum));\n    return 0;\n}\n",
      "path": "src/solution.cpp"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Replacing scanf-based input parsing with a custom fast integer reader reduces I/O overhead and ensures contiguous data ingestion into the flat matrix array. This improves memory locality by eliminating library call overhead and allowing the CPU to stream data directly from stdin into cache-friendly storage.",
  "notes": "Fast input using getchar_unlocked should reduce runtime, especially for large N (up to 8000). The two-pass integral image and blocked search remain unchanged as they already provide good spatial locality. Block size B=256 is retained based on previous experiments.",
